comment = "WASPNest bhyve, VMM, device, checkpoint, and nested-VM qualification"

desc = <<EOD
Aggregate WASPNest qualification package for bhyve and the VMM kernel
subsystem.  It combines the VM-free device and sanitizer harnesses, VMM
ATF/Kyua tests, Alpine Linux and 5BSD live guest matrices, split and packed
VirtIO queues, multiqueue, device lifecycle, checkpoint/restore, bounded
soak, AHCI/NVMe/e82545/HDA/xHCI/framebuffer/UART/TPM/pvpanic/passthrough
activation and checkpoint policy, and Intel nested-VMX qualification.  The
waspnest-test entry point
reports unsupported guest features explicitly and treats failed, missing,
pending, environment-dependent, or unclassified required release gates as
failures rather than successful skips.
EOD
